<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113459" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάρυβδις</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,</span>
		
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Charybdis,</i> a whirlpool on
			the coast of Sicily, opposite Scylla, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.104
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				436
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				6.2
			</span></i>. 
			<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>whirlpool, gulf,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντα μίαν ἱκνεῖται χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					38
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				500
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				6.2.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph. of a
			rapacious person, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἁρπαγῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					248
				</span></i>
			 (troch.).</div>
